  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186087699,
      "id": "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09",
      "title": "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f002b0fa-7bd7-511d-b59c-6e67e4f6e495",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $CD=DC={I}_{2}$\n\n- **II.** $DE=ED={I}_{2}$\n\n- **III.** $D={C}^{-1}$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{2}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $D={C}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $DE=ED={I}_{2}.$ Computing $DE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ 8 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "5f788abd-27d3-5269-8229-75e2bf733922",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "6021dc0d-7e41-59e2-8731-e80993ba40a4",
